---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Scienteens Lab Portfolio"
  description="Jonas Evrard's portfolio of hands-on physics, educational design and outreach projects for Scienteens Lab."
  lang="en"
>
  <section class="portfolio-hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Portfolio for Scienteens Lab</p>
        <h1>From complex physics to hands-on discovery.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          I am Jonas Evrard, a physicist and secondary-school teacher. I design activities that help teenagers
          turn a prediction into a measurement—and a measurement into understanding.
        </p>
        <nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Portfolio sections">
          <a href="#selected-work">Selected work</a>
          <a href="#method">Workshop method</a>
          <a href="#role-fit">Role fit</a>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <aside class="brief" aria-label="Portfolio summary">
        <span class="brief-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <span>Focus</span>
          <strong>Physics & Sustainability</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Audience</span>
          <strong>Teenagers</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Approach</span>
          <strong>Predict · Build · Measure · Explain</strong>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="selected-work" class="section container">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p>
      <h2>Learning begins with something students can test.</h2>
      <p>These projects combine a physical question, an observable effect and a structured moment of reasoning.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="featured-project">
      <div class="project-copy">
        <p class="project-index">01 · Acoustics</p>
        <h3>Make sound visible</h3>
        <p>
          A Kundt-inspired apparatus and an interactive learning sequence for students around age 15. Learners
          predict resonant modes, observe nodes and antinodes, and use the pattern to estimate the speed of sound.
        </p>
        <div class="project-tags" aria-label="Project formats">
          <span>Physical prototype</span><span>Interactive model</span><span>Classroom sequence</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Connects a real experiment to its wave model.</li>
          <li>Makes boundary conditions visible and discussable.</li>
          <li>Uses prediction before measurement, not after it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="wave-lab" aria-label="Illustration of a standing wave in a tube">
        <div class="wave-label"><span>pressure pattern</span><span>resonant mode</span></div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 720 330" role="img" aria-label="Standing-wave pattern between two ends of a tube">
          <rect x="32" y="56" width="656" height="218" rx="18" />
          <line x1="32" y1="165" x2="688" y2="165" />
          <path class="wave wave-one" d="M32 165 C87 68 142 68 197 165 S307 262 362 165 S472 68 527 165 S637 262 688 165" />
          <path class="wave wave-two" d="M32 165 C87 262 142 262 197 165 S307 68 362 165 S472 262 527 165 S637 68 688 165" />
          <g class="nodes">
            <circle cx="32" cy="165" r="8" /><circle cx="197" cy="165" r="8" />
            <circle cx="362" cy="165" r="8" /><circle cx="527" cy="165" r="8" /><circle cx="688" cy="165" r="8" />
          </g>
        </svg>
        <div class="scale"><span>predict</span><span>observe</span><span>measure</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <div class="project-grid">
      <article class="project-card">
        <p class="project-index">02 · Statistical physics</p>
        <h3>Entropy on a chessboard</h3>
        <p>Use the distribution of possible moves to discuss uncertainty, choice and the fragility of a position.</p>
        <span class="status">Research-to-outreach concept</span>
      </article>
      <article class="project-card">
        <p class="project-index">03 · Energy & mechanics</p>
        <h3>Power in motion</h3>
        <p>Turn a bicycle, a slope and a gear ratio into direct measurements of force, power and efficiency.</p>
        <span class="status">Hands-on workshop concept</span>
      </article>
      <article class="project-card">
        <p class="project-index">04 · Scientific reasoning</p>
        <h3>Debunk with measurement</h3>
        <p>Move from a striking claim to a testable hypothesis, then examine what the evidence actually supports.</p>
        <span class="status">Short outreach format</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="method" class="method-section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-heading light">
        <p class="eyebrow">Workshop method</p>
        <h2>Research becomes an experience students can own.</h2>
        <p>A strong activity preserves the scientific idea while reducing the practical barriers around it.</p>
      </header>

      <ol class="method-steps">
        <li><span>01</span><strong>Start with research</strong><p>Identify the phenomenon and the question that makes it worth investigating.</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><strong>Make it testable</strong><p>Choose one visible variable and a result students can genuinely observe.</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><strong>Ask for a prediction</strong><p>Give learners a reason to commit to an idea before the apparatus answers.</p></li>
        <li><span>04</span><strong>Measure and compare</strong><p>Collect evidence, estimate uncertainty and confront the initial model.</p></li>
        <li><span>05</span><strong>Explain and extend</strong><p>Build the physical rule together, then test where it stops working.</p></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="design-criteria">
        <p>Every outreach setup should be:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>quick to understand</li><li>safe to manipulate</li><li>robust and resettable</li>
          <li>visually legible</li><li>open to real student decisions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container focus-section">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Physics & Sustainability</p>
      <h2>Areas prepared for the role.</h2>
      <p>
        I studied the existing workshop themes to understand both their physics and the decisions learners should
        be able to make during the activity.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="topic-list">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Solar cells</h3><p>DSSC, current–voltage curves, maximum power point and efficiency.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Power & storage</h3><p>Energy transfer, storage technologies, losses and system efficiency.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Energy-system games</h3><p>Balancing production, demand, constraints and trade-offs.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Forests & climate</h3><p>Measurements that connect local observations to carbon and climate processes.</p></article>
      <article><span>05</span><h3>Myths & evidence</h3><p>Hypothesis, measurement, bias and the limits of a conclusion.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">
      Preparation themes include <em>High-tech research for better solar cells</em>, <em>I've got the power!</em>,
      <em>Power Planner</em>, <em>What are trees up to?</em> and <em>Debunking myths with physics</em>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="role-fit" class="section container role-fit">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">What I bring</p>
      <h2>A bridge between research, teaching and making.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="fit-grid">
      <article><span>Physics</span><h3>Scientific depth</h3><p>A background in condensed matter, instrumentation, numerical analysis and medical physics.</p></article>
      <article><span>Teaching</span><h3>Learner awareness</h3><p>Daily experience turning abstract models into activities for secondary-school students.</p></article>
      <article><span>Data & code</span><h3>Tools that clarify</h3><p>Data-quality workflows, simulations and interactive resources built around the scientific question.</p></article>
      <article><span>Outreach</span><h3>Short, memorable formats</h3><p>Activities designed to remain meaningful when time, space and attention are limited.</p></article>
    </div>

    <blockquote>
      <p>“The learner should not watch science happen. They should have a decision to make before it happens.”</p>
      <footer>Jonas Evrard · Physicist and secondary-school teacher</footer>
    </blockquote>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .portfolio-hero { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 9rem); }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(18rem, 0.55fr); gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem); align-items: end; }
  h1 { max-width: 11ch; margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(3.7rem, 8vw, 7.6rem); font-weight: 760; letter-spacing: -0.07em; line-height: 0.9; }
  .lead { max-width: 47rem; margin: var(--space-5) 0 0; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: clamp(1.12rem, 2.2vw, 1.45rem); }
  .page-nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .page-nav a { padding: 0.62rem 0.85rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--color-surface); color: var(--color-primary-dark); font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 750; text-decoration: none; }
  .brief { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); padding: var(--space-5); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--color-ink); color: white; }
  .brief-number { color: var(--color-accent); font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.14em; }
  .brief div { display: grid; gap: 0.15rem; padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16); }
  .brief div span { color: #aebdb6; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .brief strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.25; }
  .section { padding-block: var(--space-7); }
  .section-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(17rem, 0.55fr); column-gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem); align-items: end; margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .section-heading .eyebrow { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .section-heading h2 { max-width: 16ch; margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.7rem); letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 0.98; }
  .section-heading > p:not(.eyebrow) { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .featured-project { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(23rem, 1.15fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem); padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); border: 1px solid var(--color-line); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--color-surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft); }
  .project-index { margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); color: var(--color-primary); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: 0.11em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .project-copy h3, .project-card h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.045em; line-height: 1; }
  .project-copy h3 { font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 5vw, 4.2rem); }
  .project-copy > p:not(.project-index) { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 1.08rem; }
  .project-copy ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; }
  .project-copy li + li { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .project-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); margin-block: var(--space-4); }
  .project-tags span, .status { display: inline-block; padding: 0.35rem 0.55rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--color-surface-strong); color: var(--color-primary-dark); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 750; }
  .wave-lab { display: grid; align-content: space-between; min-height: 29rem; padding: var(--space-4); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-ink); color: white; }
  .wave-label, .scale { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; color: #aebdb6; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .wave-lab svg { width: 100%; }
  .wave-lab rect { fill: none; stroke: #42564e; stroke-width: 2; }
  .wave-lab line { stroke: #42564e; stroke-dasharray: 5 7; }
  .wave { fill: none; stroke-width: 4; }
  .wave-one { stroke: var(--color-accent); }
  .wave-two { stroke: #65c2aa; }
  .nodes circle { fill: var(--color-surface); }
  .project-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-4); margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .project-card { display: grid; min-height: 20rem; padding: var(--space-5); border: 1px solid var(--color-line); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: rgba(255, 253, 248, 0.7); }
  .project-card h3 { font-size: 2rem; }
  .project-card > p:not(.project-index) { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .project-card .status { align-self: end; justify-self: start; }
  .method-section { padding-block: var(--space-7); background: var(--color-ink); color: white; }
  .section-heading.light h2 { color: white; }
  .section-heading.light > p:not(.eyebrow) { color: #b7c5be; }
  .method-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); padding: 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; border-block: 1px solid #42564e; }
  .method-steps li { min-height: 18rem; padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid #42564e; }
  .method-steps li:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .method-steps span { color: var(--color-accent); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 850; }
  .method-steps strong { display: block; margin-top: 5rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.1; }
  .method-steps p { color: #b7c5be; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .design-criteria { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.55fr 1.45fr; gap: var(--space-5); margin-top: var(--space-5); align-items: start; }
  .design-criteria > p { margin: 0; color: #b7c5be; }
  .design-criteria ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); padding: 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .design-criteria li { padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem; border: 1px solid #42564e; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
  .focus-section { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .topic-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .topic-list article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4rem minmax(12rem, 0.55fr) minmax(15rem, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); padding-block: var(--space-4); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); align-items: baseline; }
  .topic-list article > span { color: var(--color-primary); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 850; }
  .topic-list h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.035em; }
  .topic-list p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .source-note { max-width: var(--text-width); margin: var(--space-5) 0 0 auto; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.86rem; }
  .fit-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--color-line); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--color-line); }
  .fit-grid article { min-height: 16rem; padding: var(--space-5); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .fit-grid span { color: var(--color-primary); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .fit-grid h3 { margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; letter-spacing: -0.04em; }
  .fit-grid p { max-width: 32rem; margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); }
  blockquote { margin: var(--space-7) 0 0; padding-left: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); border-left: 5px solid var(--color-accent); }
  blockquote p { max-width: 25ch; margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem); letter-spacing: -0.05em; line-height: 1.05; }
  blockquote footer { margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }

  @media (max-width: 62rem) {
    .method-steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .method-steps li { border-bottom: 1px solid #42564e; }
    .method-steps li:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
    .method-steps li:last-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; min-height: 13rem; }
    .method-steps strong { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 50rem) {
    .hero-grid, .section-heading, .featured-project { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .section-heading > p:not(.eyebrow) { margin-top: var(--space-4); }
    .project-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .project-card { min-height: 16rem; }
    .topic-list article { grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr; }
    .topic-list p { grid-column: 2; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 38rem) {
    .page-nav { display: grid; }
    .method-steps, .fit-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .method-steps li, .method-steps li:nth-child(2n) { min-height: auto; border-right: 0; }
    .method-steps li:last-child { grid-column: auto; }
    .design-criteria { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .wave-lab { min-height: 20rem; }
  }
</style>
